# Declare

Author a card in Python and write it to disk. Each card class owns its local
`save`/`load`; the card envelope on disk is what you register.

<Aside title="Registration uses Cards" data-variant="wyrd">

The Python package exposes a tenant-scoped `Cards` client. Use
`cards.data.register`, `cards.model.register`, or `cards.prompt.register` for
Python-authored holders. Use the matching `get` method to retrieve the
server-persisted envelope; call `DataCard.load` or `ModelCard.load` when you
also need the registered artifacts.

</Aside>

## Shipped kinds

- [Declare a Prompt card](/how-to/declare/prompt/)
- [Declare a Model card](/how-to/declare/model/)
- [Declare a Data card](/how-to/declare/data/)

## Reserved kinds

The other thirteen card kinds (Agent, Service, Workflow, Eval, Experiment,
Drift, Audit, Policy, Trigger, Mcp, Operator, Artifact, Source) have authored
contracts and JSON Schemas, but their runtime implementation is not shipped yet.
How-to pages for these kinds will be added as each kind's contract ships.

See [Cards](/cards/) for the full catalog and shipping status.

## Complete Service bundles

For an offline handoff, use the CLI's complete Service `get` output rather than
the metadata-only mode. The complete bundle contains the sorted manifest,
Card envelopes, relationships, and verified artifact payloads. Load it with
`WyrdState.from_path(path)` and provide interfaces only for custom loaders;
built-in Data and trusted Model loaders run during construction. Agent and
Workflow entries remain declarative envelope projections in this offline state.
